==English==

===Etymology===
Possibly from {{term|wiseacre}}, influenced by {{term|pillock}}, or possibly {{suffix|wazz|ock|lang=en}}. First attested in the 1984 novel ''When the Martians Land in Huddersfield'' by Mike Harding.<ref>Alex Games, ''Balderdash and Piffle'' (2010), page 242</ref><ref>[http://www.independent.co.uk/news/uk/home-news/shaggy-dog-story-of-our-strangest-expressions-397268.html "wazzock", listed as a stupid or annoying person, was found in a 1976 recording by the British folk singer, author and broadcaster Mike Harding]</ref>

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{label|en|British|chiefly|Northern England|mildly|pejorative|slang}} A [[stupid]] or [[annoying]] person.

